Subject: [PATCH] feat(lists): the Excel says who among your contacts fits each
 row's need (4160)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tester 49306 (goal 23728): a file of „name, need" rows. The chat named a
contact of the owner for four of the five needs („ბუღალტერი: შენს
კონტაქტებში არის ლევან ბუღალტერი…"); the Excel said „შენს კონტაქტებში
არავინ" five times. Both were right about different questions: the list
engine answers who leads to the PERSON in the row, and the chat answered
who fits the row's NEED.

When the file has a need column (need, საჭიროება, რა სჭირდება, потребность,
necesidad), the workbook gains one more column, „Netai: საჭიროებაში
დაგეხმარება": up to three of the owner's own contacts that fit the need,
by the same own-label search the chat uses. One lookup per distinct need,
at most 60 per download. Read-only. A file with no need column is
unchanged.

DONE WHEN: the tester's „name, need" file on a fresh seat — the Excel
names, for each need, the contact the chat named.

